Aether: installer UX

Offline NSIS stub flow, welcome gate, splash, modern UI, setup icon.

Squashed from 1 units:

  [core/35-installer-ux.patch]
  Aether: installer UX
  
  Everything the user sees while Aether installs, in one patch because it only
  makes sense together:
  
  * the Add/Remove Programs entry reads "Aether Browser", the distribution
    version and "Aether Group" as publisher, with no locale in the name;
  * a welcome gate asks before starting, with a Cancel that exits instead of
    leaving the window hanging;
  * the "Welcome" splash fades in, holds and fades out before the heading and
    buttons appear;
  * the pages are actually styled. They render in the legacy IE document mode
    NSIS hosts, so this uses inline-block buttons, 6px radii, solid fills and
    opacity fades: nothing that IE lacks, and no CSS transitions;
  * the Cancel button is red, so the destructive choice reads as one;
  * typography is Quicksand Bold for titles and Comfortaa for body and buttons,
    both SIL Open Font License. The WOFFs ride next to each page's assets;
  * the installer gets its own icon. setup-stub.exe is what ships as
    AetherSetup-<version>.exe and it was compiled with the browser's flame, so
    Setup wore the same mark as the browser.
  
  The icon on the shipped file comes from the prebuilt 7z SFX module, not from
  NSIS: make-stub-offline.py concatenates the SFX with the config and the
  payload, and Windows reads the icon off the result. scripts/patch-sfx-stub.py
  rewrites that module's resources.
  diff --git a/browser/installer/windows/Makefile.in b/browser/installer/windows/Makefile.in
